# Evanio.ai

AI marketing SaaS for US small businesses.

## Structure (monorepo)

- `frontend/web`: Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui. Public site + user dashboard. Deployed on Vercel.
- `frontend/admin`: separate Next.js app for admins only. Deployed on Vercel at admin.evanio.ai.
- `backend`: Node.js + TypeScript + Hono. Deployed on Railway. BullMQ + Redis for background jobs.
- `supabase`: SQL migrations. Supabase for Postgres, Auth, Storage.

## Rules

- Frontend never holds secret keys. Only `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`.
- All AI calls, credit deduction, Stripe and Meta logic happen ONLY in the backend.
- Frontend calls backend with the Supabase access token in the Authorization header; backend verifies it.
- Use zod for validation. Use environment variables, never hardcode keys.
- Keep code modular: routes -> services. Small files, clear names.
- Every new table has Row Level Security enabled.
- Ask before deleting files or changing the folder structure.
